-- 2. crashes15   : count DISTINCT crashes in 2015 per state_number after excluding the
--                  three “non-informative” distraction labels.
-- 3. crashes16   : same logic for 2016.
-- 4. combined    : FULL OUTER JOIN the two yearly tables on state_number so every
--                  state that appears in either year is included.  Use COALESCE to
--                  keep a single state_number column; IFNULL() converts missing counts
--                  to zeros.
-- 5. Final step  : CROSS JOIN with pop (because pop has no state_number) and compute
--                  crash rates for both years.  Order by 2015 rate descending, then 2016.
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT SUM(`population`) AS us_pop_2010
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_usa.population_by_zip_2010`
